@page "/betting-101"
@using SportsBettingAnalyzer.Components.Shared.Tailwind
@rendermode InteractiveServer

<TwContainer>
    <!-- Page Header -->
    <div class="text-center mb-16">
        <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-black text-white mb-6 tracking-tight">🎓 Sports Betting 101</h1>
        <p class="text-xl text-slate-400 max-w-2xl mx-auto">
            Learn how to leverage math and logic to beat the sportsbooks and bet efficiently.
        </p>
    </div>

    <TwGrid Columns="1" ColumnsMd="2" Gap="8" Class="mb-12">
        @* 1. Bankroll Management *@
        <TwCard Class="h-full border-l-4 border-l-blue-500 bg-slate-900 shadow-xl overflow-hidden hover:scale-[1.02] transition-transform duration-300">
            <div class="p-6">
                <div class="flex items-center gap-4 mb-6">
                    <div class="p-3 bg-blue-500/10 rounded-xl">
                        <TwIcon Icon="M3 6l3 12h12l3-12H3zm5 8h8" Class="w-8 h-8 text-blue-500" />
                    </div>
                    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white">Bankroll Management</h2>
                </div>
                
                <p class="text-slate-300 mb-6 leading-relaxed">
                    The single most important skill in betting is <strong class="text-white">preservation of capital</strong>. Without a bankroll, you can't place bets.
                </p>

                <ul class="space-y-4">
                    <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
                        <TwIcon Icon="M9 12l2 2 4-4m6 2a9 9 0 11-18 0 9 9 0 0118 0z" Class="w-5 h-5 text-emerald-500 mt-1 flex-shrink-0" />
                        <span class="text-slate-400"><strong class="text-slate-200">The 1-3% Rule:</strong> Never bet more than 1-3% of your total bankroll on a single game.</span>
                    </li>
                    <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
                        <TwIcon Icon="M9 12l2 2 4-4m6 2a9 9 0 11-18 0 9 9 0 0118 0z" Class="w-5 h-5 text-emerald-500 mt-1 flex-shrink-0" />
                        <span class="text-slate-400"><strong class="text-slate-200">Standardize Units:</strong> Define a "Unit" (e.g., $10 or $100) and track your profit in units, not dollars.</span>
                    </li>
                    <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
                        <TwIcon Icon="M12 8v4m0 4h.01M21 12a9 9 0 11-18 0 9 9 0 0118 0z" Class="w-5 h-5 text-red-500 mt-1 flex-shrink-0" />
                        <span class="text-slate-400"><strong class="text-slate-200">Don't Chase:</strong> Increasing your bet size to "get even" after a loss is the fastest way to go broke.</span>
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </TwCard>

        @* 2. Expected Value (EV+) *@
        <TwCard Class="h-full border-l-4 border-l-purple-500 bg-slate-900 shadow-xl overflow-hidden hover:scale-[1.02] transition-transform duration-300">
            <div class="p-6">
                <div class="flex items-center gap-4 mb-6">
                    <div class="p-3 bg-purple-500/10 rounded-xl">
                        <TwIcon Icon="M9 7h6m0 10v-3m-3 3h.01M9 17h.01M9 14h.01M12 14h.01M15 11h.01M12 11h.01M9 11h.01M7 21h10a2 2 0 002-2V5a2 2 0 00-2-2H7a2 2 0 00-2 2v14a2 2 0 002 2z" Class="w-8 h-8 text-purple-500" />
                    </div>
                    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white">Positive Expected Value (EV+)</h2>
                </div>
                
                <p class="text-slate-300 mb-6 leading-relaxed">
                    EV betting is when the <strong class="text-white">probability of winning</strong> is higher than the <strong class="text-white">implied probability</strong> of the odds.
                </p>

                <div class="bg-indigo-500/10 border border-indigo-500/20 rounded-xl p-4 mb-6">
                    <p class="text-indigo-300 font-mono text-sm text-center">Formula: (Win Prob * Payout) - (Loss Prob * Stake)</p>
                </div>

                <p class="text-slate-400 text-sm italic">
                    If the result is positive, it's a "math win" long-term. Our models specialize in finding these discrepancies between reality and sportsbook lines.
                </p>
            </div>
        </TwCard>

        @* 3. Understanding Odds *@
        <TwCard Class="h-full border-l-4 border-l-amber-500 bg-slate-900 shadow-xl overflow-hidden hover:scale-[1.02] transition-transform duration-300">
            <div class="p-6">
                <div class="flex items-center gap-4 mb-6">
                    <div class="p-3 bg-amber-500/10 rounded-xl">
                        <TwIcon Icon="M9 19v-6a2 2 0 00-2-2H5a2 2 0 00-2 2v6a2 2 0 002 2h2a2 2 0 002-2zm0 0V9a2 2 0 012-2h2a2 2 0 012 2v10m-6 0a2 2 0 002 2h2a2 2 0 002-2m0 0V5a2 2 0 012-2h2a2 2 0 012 2v14a2 2 0 01-2 2h-2a2 2 0 01-2-2z" Class="w-8 h-8 text-amber-500" />
                    </div>
                    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white">Understanding Odds</h2>
                </div>
                
                <p class="text-slate-300 mb-6 leading-relaxed">
                    Odds are just <strong class="text-white">probabilities</strong> in disguise.
                </p>

                <div class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-4">
                    <div class="p-3 bg-slate-800/50 rounded-lg">
                        <h4 class="text-xs font-black text-slate-500 uppercase tracking-widest mb-2">American Odds</h4>
                        <p class="text-xs text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">-110: Bet $110 to win $100.<br/>+150: Bet $100 to win $150.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="p-3 bg-slate-800/50 rounded-lg">
                        <h4 class="text-xs font-black text-slate-500 uppercase tracking-widest mb-2">Implied Prob</h4>
                        <p class="text-xs text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">-110 = 52.4% chance.<br/>+100 = 50.0% chance.<br/>+200 = 33.3% chance.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </TwCard>

        @* 4. The Kelly Criterion *@
        <TwCard Class="h-full border-l-4 border-l-emerald-500 bg-slate-900 shadow-xl overflow-hidden hover:scale-[1.02] transition-transform duration-300">
            <div class="p-6">
                <div class="flex items-center gap-4 mb-6">
                    <div class="p-3 bg-emerald-500/10 rounded-xl">
                        <TwIcon Icon="M3 6l3 12h12l3-12H3zm5 8h8" Class="w-8 h-8 text-emerald-500" />
                    </div>
                    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white">The Kelly Criterion</h2>
                </div>
                
                <p class="text-slate-300 mb-6 leading-relaxed">
                    The Kelly Criterion is a formula used to determine the <strong class="text-white">mathematically optimal amount</strong> to bet on a simulation.
                </p>

                <div class="p-4 bg-emerald-500/5 border border-emerald-500/10 rounded-xl italic text-center text-emerald-400 text-sm mb-6">
                    "Bet more when the edge is high, bet less when the edge is low."
                </div>

                <div class="flex items-start gap-3 text-slate-400 text-xs bg-emerald-500/5 p-3 rounded-lg">
                    <TwIcon Icon="M13 16h-1v-4h-1m1-4h.01M21 12a9 9 0 11-18 0 9 9 0 0118 0z" Class="w-5 h-5 text-emerald-500 flex-shrink-0" />
                    Our app calculates this automatically in the <strong class="text-slate-200">Live Odds</strong> pages to help you size your stakes.
                </div>
            </div>
        </TwCard>
    </TwGrid>

    @* Quick Tips Section *@
    <TwCard Class="mb-12 bg-slate-900 border-slate-800 overflow-hidden">
        <div class="p-8">
            <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-8 flex items-center gap-3">
                <TwIcon Icon="M13 10V3L4 14h7v7l9-11h-7z" Class="w-6 h-6 text-yellow-400" />
                ⚡ Pro Tips for Efficiency
            </h3>
            <TwGrid Columns="1" ColumnsSm="3" Gap="8">
                <div>
                    <h4 class="text-lg font-bold text-white mb-2">Line Shopping</h4>
                    <p class="text-sm text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">Always check multiple sportsbooks. Getting FanDuel at -105 vs DraftKings at -110 adds up to a huge difference over 1,000 bets.</p>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <h4 class="text-lg font-bold text-white mb-2">Avoid the "Parlay Trap"</h4>
                    <p class="text-sm text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">Parlays are highly profitable for books. Use them sparingly or only when every leg has positive EV (Correlation is key!).</p>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <h4 class="text-lg font-bold text-white mb-2">Trust the Data</h4>
                    <p class="text-sm text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">Model logic is superior to "gut feelings." If the XGBoost and Neural Network agree, it's a high-conviction signal.</p>
                </div>
            </TwGrid>
        </div>
    </TwCard>

    <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row justify-center gap-4 py-8">
        <TwButton Variant="primary" Href="/live-nba-odds" Size="lg" Class="px-8">
            <TwIcon Icon="M13 10V3L4 14h7v7l9-11h-7z" Class="w-5 h-5 mr-3" />
            Apply to NBA
        </TwButton>
        <TwButton Variant="secondary" Href="/live-nfl-odds" Size="lg" Class="px-8">
            <TwIcon Icon="M13 10V3L4 14h7v7l9-11h-7z" Class="w-5 h-5 mr-3" />
            Apply to NFL
        </TwButton>
    </div>
</TwContainer>

